WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.320
Your engagement with the score is to&nbsp;
attempt to overcome it in a way, isn't it?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:13.280
the score is to be big and so you're finding&nbsp;
how you can be – how I can make the biggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:20.480
shape I possibly can within the refrains of&nbsp;
the grammar or the score or the framework.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:29.200
So it kind of puts the framework at the front&nbsp;
to allow you to see the play that can happen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:40.880
around it, and I think that brings a different&nbsp;
relationship with the idea of all of that – like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:51.120
regulations, design – that they're not things&nbsp;
that we have to accept and silently negotiate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.840
but that the negotiation and noticing of&nbsp;
them can be the artwork itself almost.

